  {
   "id": "eld60ve2alkysa",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 800,
   "y": 1300,
   "width": 803.88,
   "height": 227.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": "el1c0nrlil7olm",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1903338841,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1495088818,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "\u00b7 Groq free rejects ANY request > 8,000 tokens; our run prompts are p50 12.6K \u2192 Groq can't execute,\n  but fits reviews (judge p90 6.4K) \u2192 cross-family reviewer.\n\u00b7 Gemini 3 returns HTTP 400 if a tool call's thought_signature is not sent back; the value\n  'skip_thought_signature_validator' is accepted for history written by another model\n  \u2192 lane switches into Gemini are safe.\n\u00b7 Gemini free returned 503 'high demand' and one request hung > 90 s \u2192 short timeouts + failover.\n\u00b7 Gemini quota is per Google project, not per key \u2192 two keys from one project add nothing.\n\u00b7 Free quotas count REQUESTS \u2192 fewer, fatter calls (parallel reads, multi-file patches).\n\u00b7 Limits change without notice (Google cut free quotas 50\u201380% in Dec 2025)\n  \u2192 registry values are only seeds; real limits are learned from headers and 429 bodies.\n\u00b7 Switching model loses the prompt cache (~90% of our tokens are cached)\n  \u2192 router is sticky, switches only on unavailability or escalation.\n\u00b7 Keys are NEVER pooled across users: lane.owner \u2208 {this user, platform}.",
   "originalText": "\u00b7 Groq free rejects ANY request > 8,000 tokens; our run prompts are p50 12.6K \u2192 Groq can't execute,\n  but fits reviews (judge p90 6.4K) \u2192 cross-family reviewer.\n\u00b7 Gemini 3 returns HTTP 400 if a tool call's thought_signature is not sent back; the value\n  'skip_thought_signature_validator' is accepted for history written by another model\n  \u2192 lane switches into Gemini are safe.\n\u00b7 Gemini free returned 503 'high demand' and one request hung > 90 s \u2192 short timeouts + failover.\n\u00b7 Gemini quota is per Google project, not per key \u2192 two keys from one project add nothing.\n\u00b7 Free quotas count REQUESTS \u2192 fewer, fatter calls (parallel reads, multi-file patches).\n\u00b7 Limits change without notice (Google cut free quotas 50\u201380% in Dec 2025)\n  \u2192 registry values are only seeds; real limits are learned from headers and 429 bodies.\n\u00b7 Switching model loses the prompt cache (~90% of our tokens are cached)\n  \u2192 router is sticky, switches only on unavailability or escalation.\n\u00b7 Keys are NEVER pooled across users: lane.owner \u2208 {this user, platform}.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
